"""An actual route index with edition decisions, not a placeholder landing page."""
P='/d2-survivors/'
def home(shell,ext,figure):
 cards=[('play/','Play in a game window','Load the older hosted edition on click; keep its host and saves separate.','01'),('beginners-guide/','Start your first run','Class selector or camp? Follow the menu your version actually shows.','02'),('setup/','Prepare the original','Choose browser files or the desktop app, with the author’s Steam Deck route.','03'),('saves/','Find your saved run','Check Continue, the hero and the host before importing or starting fresh.','04'),('druid-skills/','Rest a skill or rebuild?','Separate unwanted casts from a re-draft, and protect the saved run first.','05'),('attack-speed/','Compare IAS with cast rate','Use Survivors speed rules instead of copying Diablo II breakpoints.','06'),('zh/localization/','繁體中文化','瀏覽器書籤與Windows工具怎麼選；先備份，再看版本與手機限制。','07'),('ko/','디아2 뱀서 시작 안내','원본과 호스팅 버전, 설치 경로와 저장 데이터부터 확인하세요.','08')]
 body=f'''<header class="d2-hero" id="guide"><div><span class="d2-eyebrow">INDEPENDENT GAME GUIDE · FRAMARA’S FAN PROJECT</span><h1>D2 Survivors</h1><p class="d2-deck">Diablo II roots.<br>A different kind of run.</p><p>Move through the horde, let skills attack and shape the next upgrade. Start with the right edition, then find your next decision.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="{P}play/">Play in a game window →</a><a class="button secondary" href="{P}beginners-guide/">Start here →</a></div><p class="d2-source">Want the current original? {ext('https://d2survivors.lol/','D2 Survivors · original project')} [1]</p></div><div class="d2-hero-media">{figure('druid-select','Druid selected among the original D2 Survivors heroes','Original hero-selector interface, captured 3 November 2026. Game art © Blizzard Entertainment / respective owners. Interface inspection, not a build ranking.',2)}</div></header>
<div class="d2-strip"><span>01 · CHOOSE A HOST</span><span>02 · LEARN THE MENU</span><span>03 · KEEP A BACKUP</span></div>
<section class="section" id="guides"><p class="d2-eyebrow">THE FIELD INDEX</p><h2>What are you trying to do?</h2><div class="d2-cards">'''
 for slug,title,desc,n in cards:body+=f'<a class="d2-card" href="{P+slug}"'+(' lang="zh-Hant"'if slug.startswith('zh/')else' lang="ko"'if slug=='ko/'else'')+f'><span class="d2-number">{n}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{desc}</p><span class="d2-card-action">Open guide →</span></a>'
 body+='''</div></section><section class="section" id="versions"><p class="d2-eyebrow">CHOOSE BEFORE YOU IMPORT</p><h2>One name does not mean one version</h2><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="D2 Survivors editions"><table><thead><tr><th>What you found</th><th>What this guide means</th><th>Where to go</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Framara’s original</td><td>The fan project at d2survivors.lol, with its own browser and desktop routes. Its current FAQ asks for your own Diablo II or D2R installation.</td><td><a href="/d2-survivors/setup/">Prepare the original →</a></td></tr><tr><td>Our Play window</td><td>A third-party edition from play.d2survivors.org. Its menu and run display older, differing build labels. It is not presented as the current original.</td><td><a href="/d2-survivors/play/">Read the host notice and play →</a></td></tr><tr><td>zombodotcom’s Windows project</td><td>Another publisher’s D2 Survivors project, with its own launcher and mode descriptions. Do not assume our original-game instructions or saves apply.</td><td>Follow that project’s own page [3]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Bring a backup, not an assumption of compatibility. A name match, familiar Diablo art or an identical button does not prove that two websites share progress. [1][2][3]</p></section>
<div class="d2-note-grid"><section class="section" id="start"><h2>Start with the screen in front of you</h2><p>The checked original menu displayed build 20261102.2 and a class selector. Current reference pages also describe a camp and waypoint. Our <a href="/d2-survivors/beginners-guide/">beginner guide</a> gives both branches, so you do not hunt an older menu for a newer control. [2][4]</p></section><section class="section" id="choices"><h2>Fix the decision before replacing a build</h2><p>Trying to stop one Druid cast? <a href="/d2-survivors/druid-skills/">Resting and re-drafting are different operations</a>. Comparing two speed items? <a href="/d2-survivors/attack-speed/">IAS and FCR share a system here</a>. These pages answer specific player questions; they are not a universal best-build list.</p></section><section class="section" id="platforms"><h2>Browser, desktop and phones</h2><p>The original offers browser and desktop routes. Its setup warns that temporary hosted files are going away; its FAQ currently recommends a computer. Older phone reports can describe a different transition state. A mobile app request, a home-screen shortcut and a verified native app are different things. <a href="/d2-survivors/setup/">Choose the supported setup path</a>. [1][4]</p><p>Hardcore and a ladder are listed by the original, but neither establishes co-op. Follow the game’s current mode descriptions rather than treating a leaderboard as multiplayer. [1]</p></section><section class="section" id="languages"><h2>Find the right language task</h2><p lang="zh-Hant">「暗黑倖存者」「D2 倖存者」可能指這款同人遊戲；本體漢化不適用。<a href="/d2-survivors/zh/localization/">繁體中文化工具與備份 →</a></p><p lang="ko"><a href="/d2-survivors/ko/">디아2 뱀서／D2 서바이버: 원본, 설치와 저장 →</a></p></section><section class="section" id="updates"><h2>Read the build before following old advice</h2><p>Checked 3 November 2026. NEWS on the original menu is the project’s own change entry. Our interface captures and mechanics references keep their dates separately; a new menu build does not automatically validate every guide. [2][4]</p></section><section class="section" id="more-games"><h2>Other games, separate progress</h2><p><a href="/azeroth-survivors/">Azeroth Survivors</a> brings a Warcraft-inspired survival loop; <a href="/soulstone-survivors/">Soulstone Survivors</a> has its own skill-chain decisions; <a href="/pokebonk/">PokeBonk</a> starts with Pokémon partners. Their developers, rules and saves are separate.</p></section></div>'''
 sources=[('https://d2survivors.lol/faq/','D2 Survivors · original FAQ','Identity, platforms and mode boundaries; checked 3 November 2026.'),('https://d2survivors.lol/play/','D2 Survivors · original browser game','Actual interface capture and displayed menu build 20261102.2. No completed run or account migration claim.'),('https://zombodotcom.github.io/d2survivors-releases/','GitHub Pages · zombodotcom project','Separate publisher and launcher; identity check, not an installation test.'),('https://d2survivors.lol/wiki/getting-started/','D2 Survivors · original reference','Current camp/waypoint and file transition documentation; can differ from the observed playable build.')]
 body+='<section class="sources" id="sources"><h2>Sources &amp; verification</h2><p>By Megabonk.org editors · 3 November 2026. This is an independent game guide, not a Blizzard or developer website. Reference pages from one project share one publisher. Version and test limits are stated on each task page.</p><ol>'+''.join(f'<li id="source-{i}">{ext(u,l)} — {d}</li>'for i,(u,l,d)in enumerate(sources,1))+'</ol><a href="#guide">Back to guide ↑</a></section>'
 # Keep source references local and light throughout this research-style index.
 import re
 body=re.sub(r'(?<![>\w-])\[(\d+)\]',lambda m:f'<sup class="ref"><a href="#source-{m[1]}">[{m[1]}]</a></sup>',body)
 return shell(P,'D2 Survivors Guides: Play, Setup, Skills & Saves','Find the right D2 Survivors edition, play in a browser window, prepare your game files and follow guides for starting, saving, Druid skills and speed stats.',body).replace('original-menu-1280.webp','druid-select-1280.webp').replace('loading="lazy"','loading="eager"',1)
